WEBVTT

1
00:54:09.226 --> 00:54:11.226
Lord, we love you.

2
00:54:13.226 --> 00:54:15.226
We love to worship you.

3
00:54:26.226 --> 00:54:29.226
Help us by your Spirit to worship you more.

4
00:54:33.226 --> 00:54:37.226
We need your Spirit to worship you in the right way.

5
00:54:39.226 --> 00:54:42.226
We need the help of your Spirit to do all things.

6
00:54:44.226 --> 00:54:46.226
Even to magnify you.

7
00:54:47.226 --> 00:54:49.226
So help us, Lord.

8
00:54:51.226 --> 00:54:53.226
Release more of your Spirit in us.

9
00:54:56.226 --> 00:54:58.226
A greater measure of your anointing upon us.

10
00:55:00.226 --> 00:55:02.226
So that we may be a house of your glory.

11
00:55:03.226 --> 00:55:05.226
A house of your presence.

12
00:55:09.226 --> 00:55:13.226
A house where worship and prayer rise day and night and night and day.

13
00:55:16.226 --> 00:55:19.226
Where people are filled with the fire of your presence.

14
00:55:22.226 --> 00:55:25.226
Where they are refreshed in the power of your presence.

15
00:55:28.226 --> 00:55:30.226
Where we are renewed in our minds.

16
00:55:32.226 --> 00:55:34.226
By the power of the words.

17
00:55:38.226 --> 00:55:40.226
And by the anointing of the Spirit.

18
00:55:43.226 --> 00:55:45.226
Lord, we need you more.

19
00:55:47.226 --> 00:55:48.226
So open our eyes.

20
00:55:49.226 --> 00:55:50.226
Open our hearts.

21
00:55:52.226 --> 00:55:53.226
Reveal who you are.

22
00:55:56.226 --> 00:55:58.226
In a greater way today.

23
00:56:02.226 --> 00:56:04.226
Let's give the Lord a round of applause.

24
00:56:09.226 --> 00:56:11.226
Let the band give a round of applause.

25
00:56:16.226 --> 00:56:17.226
Please take a seat.

26
00:56:25.226 --> 00:56:28.226
And we've already said, next Sunday is the big celebration.

27
00:56:38.226 --> 00:56:39.226
He is watching everything.

28
00:56:40.226 --> 00:56:41.226
Amen.

29
00:56:42.226 --> 00:56:43.226
Amen.

30
00:56:44.226 --> 00:56:45.226
And look.

31
00:56:47.226 --> 00:56:48.226
I have a hard S.

32
00:56:49.226 --> 00:56:51.226
When I say S, it is very sharp.

33
00:56:52.226 --> 00:56:54.226
So I get this to help me.

34
00:56:54.226 --> 00:56:55.226
Amen.

35
00:56:57.226 --> 00:56:59.226
I’m just letting you in on all these little things.

36
00:57:00.226 --> 00:57:01.226
So next week is...

37
00:57:02.226 --> 00:57:03.226
And I think it's great that Rachel just stops.

38
00:57:03.226 --> 00:57:04.226
Because she is just rattling.

39
00:57:05.226 --> 00:57:06.226
So I won't read over it.

40
00:57:06.226 --> 00:57:10.226
Only the secrets know what I'm saying now.

41
00:57:10.226 --> 00:57:11.226
Okay.

42
00:57:12.226 --> 00:57:13.226
Next week...

43
00:57:13.226 --> 00:57:15.226
Yes, I have a bit of a nose today.

44
00:57:15.226 --> 00:57:16.226
So stay with me.

45
00:57:20.226 --> 00:57:21.226
I need a bit more water.

46
00:57:22.226 --> 00:57:24.226
Next week is our celebration.

47
00:57:27.226 --> 00:57:31.226
But we are also celebrating the coming of the Spirit next weekend.

48
00:57:31.226 --> 00:57:35.226
But next week is also the feast of the coming of the Spirit.

49
00:57:37.226 --> 00:57:39.226
And we really don't want to miss that.

50
00:57:43.226 --> 00:57:46.226
You never know. If we have a barbecue, the Spirit might come upon us.

51
00:57:54.226 --> 00:57:57.226
That we talk about prayer and fasting.

52
00:57:57.226 --> 00:58:00.226
And then while we are barbecuing, the Spirit comes with fire.

53
00:58:02.226 --> 00:58:05.226
While we are barbecuing, the Spirit falls.

54
00:58:06.226 --> 00:58:07.226
That is also possible.

55
00:58:08.226 --> 00:58:09.226
All possible.

56
00:58:10.226 --> 00:58:11.226
It's okay Rakel, you can read over it.

57
00:58:12.226 --> 00:58:14.226
I'm going in.

58
00:58:15.226 --> 00:58:19.226
But I want to learn it today.

59
00:58:19.226 --> 00:58:23.226
The coming of the Spirit and His ministry in and through us.

60
00:58:23.226 --> 00:58:29.226
I want to speak today about the coming of the Spirit and His ministry in us and through us.

61
00:58:30.226 --> 00:58:38.226
The coming of the Spirit means that there is more to do and that we can do more.

62
00:58:44.226 --> 00:58:45.226
I will say it again.

63
00:58:45.226 --> 00:58:49.226
The coming of the Spirit was because there was more to do.

64
00:58:54.226 --> 00:58:56.226
And so that more could be done.

65
00:58:57.226 --> 00:59:01.226
Do you remember, last week Tim talked about Jesus here on earth.

66
00:59:19.226 --> 00:59:21.226
Jesus was in a physical body here on earth.

67
00:59:27.226 --> 00:59:31.226
And Jesus limited himself for a time and for a season.

68
00:59:40.226 --> 00:59:45.226
That means that during the time he was here on earth, he was physically present where he was.

69
00:59:45.226 --> 00:59:50.226
And just like me, if I am in this room, I cannot be in the room next door.

70
00:59:51.226 --> 00:59:56.226
And he was completely dependent on the Father in prayer.

71
00:59:59.226 --> 01:00:00.226
And the Spirit upon him.

72
01:00:02.226 --> 01:00:04.226
To do the will of the Father.

73
01:00:12.226 --> 01:00:17.226
Jesus said, I do nothing without first seeing the Father do it in prayer.

74
01:00:18.226 --> 01:00:20.226
And that is very efficient.

75
01:00:38.226 --> 01:00:44.226
It is very efficient and you see that Jesus healed everyone who came to him.

76
01:00:44.226 --> 01:00:47.226
But he did not heal everyone, he healed everyone who came.

77
01:00:55.226 --> 01:00:59.226
And Jesus showed us what it is to truly be a Son of God.

78
01:01:04.226 --> 01:01:09.226
It was intended that Adam lived in that way in the garden with the Father.

79
01:01:11.226 --> 01:01:13.226
With the presence of the Lord.

80
01:01:15.226 --> 01:01:17.226
To have dominion over the earth.

81
01:01:24.226 --> 01:01:30.226
But Jesus has shown us what it really was to live as a true Son of God here on earth.

82
01:01:30.226 --> 01:01:39.226
And then Tim talked about how he went up to heaven from the Mount of Olives, that he ascended, that they saw him go up.

83
01:01:47.226 --> 01:01:49.226
And while they were seeing him go up,

84
01:01:56.226 --> 01:01:58.226
there stood two men in white.

85
01:02:01.226 --> 01:02:03.226
And they asked them, why are you looking up?

86
01:02:11.226 --> 01:02:18.226
The Bible also has humor, because listen, Jesus is going up there and then they ask, what are you looking at? Well, at Jesus.

87
01:02:19.226 --> 01:02:29.226
And then they said, the Jesus you see now, and I loved what you brought forth, this same Jesus, meaning physical Jesus, will return in the same way he went up.

88
01:02:36.226 --> 01:02:39.226
Do you know that he still has the scars in his hands?

89
01:02:40.226 --> 01:02:44.226
He has healed us, but he will retain the signs forever.

90
01:02:52.226 --> 01:02:56.226
Even in his glorified body, he bears the mark of salvation.

91
01:03:01.226 --> 01:03:04.226
We see that in Revelation, that the lamb has been slain.

92
01:03:10.226 --> 01:03:18.226
We see it when he returns, he comes and says, look Thomas, touch me, I am the only one who has holes in his hands.

93
01:03:18.226 --> 01:03:23.226
They were not removed when he went back to heaven.

94
01:03:31.226 --> 01:03:34.226
He is the lamb that is eternally slain.

95
01:03:34.226 --> 01:03:37.226
He is forever the lamb that has been slain.

96
01:03:56.226 --> 01:04:02.226
And in the gospel of John, Jesus says to the disciples, it is better for you that I go.

97
01:04:05.226 --> 01:04:11.226
And when I first read that passage, I really had that thought of Jesus, how can that be true, how can it be better that you go?

98
01:04:21.226 --> 01:04:24.226
But then he says, for then my spirit can come.

99
01:04:25.226 --> 01:04:31.226
When I, as a physical man, go back to the Father, then the Father and I will send our spirit to you.

100
01:04:40.226 --> 01:04:45.226
And when my spirit, the spirit of Christ, I remember that he trained us on this a few years ago.

101
01:04:45.226 --> 01:04:51.226
In the gospel of John, he says, another will come and the other means the same.

102
01:04:52.226 --> 01:05:00.226
And I talked about it a few years ago as well, but it says in John, then the other will come and that other is exactly the same as Jesus.

103
01:05:06.226 --> 01:05:08.226
The spirit is not a wind.

104
01:05:10.226 --> 01:05:12.226
Even though he moves like a wind.

105
01:05:13.226 --> 01:05:16.226
He is not just a fire, even though he is fire.

106
01:05:17.226 --> 01:05:21.226
He is not just a power, but he is powerful.

107
01:05:28.226 --> 01:05:31.226
He is truly the spirit of Jesus, the same one.

108
01:05:37.226 --> 01:05:41.226
And therefore we must honor him as the Lord in our midst.

109
01:05:47.226 --> 01:05:53.226
Of the Trinity, the spirit is the one who is most misunderstood.

110
01:05:55.226 --> 01:05:57.226
He is the one who is most ignored.

111
01:05:59.226 --> 01:06:01.226
For we cannot control him.

112
01:06:08.226 --> 01:06:15.226
And we cannot control Jesus either, but for us that is easier to imagine, the Father and the Son, but the spirit, what do we do with that?

113
01:06:17.226 --> 01:06:21.226
And I think he has a purpose in that.

114
01:06:27.226 --> 01:06:32.226
For then we must trust him and build on him in a greater way.

115
01:06:32.226 --> 01:06:57.226
And when Jesus says, it is better for you that I go, for then my spirit can come, what he is saying is that there is still much more work to be done, but that much more work can be done when the spirit is present.

116
01:06:58.226 --> 01:07:00.226
For now He is in you.

117
01:07:05.226 --> 01:07:08.226
Christ, that hope of glory, lives in you.

118
01:07:11.226 --> 01:07:14.226
And truly, if you believe that, He is in you.

119
01:07:17.226 --> 01:07:19.226
And He wants to come in a greater measure.

120
01:07:28.226 --> 01:07:36.226
And when we see in Acts that the Lord ascends, so that the spirit can come down, there is a purpose behind that.

121
01:07:37.226 --> 01:07:38.226
There is a reason.

122
01:07:46.226 --> 01:07:51.226
And then Christ says, you will now be witnesses of everything you have seen.

123
01:07:57.226 --> 01:08:26.226
And at the moment they have to choose a twelfth apostle, Peter says, it must be someone who has been there all the way, who has seen Jesus come, who has seen him die, who has seen him after his resurrection, and who has seen him ascend to heaven.

124
01:08:28.226 --> 01:08:30.226
For they must be deeply convinced.

125
01:08:39.226 --> 01:08:46.226
You cannot go to the unbelieving Jewish land and tell them about the Messiah if you are not deeply convinced yourself.

126
01:08:49.226 --> 01:08:52.226
Can I tell us that this is no different today?

127
01:08:58.226 --> 01:09:05.226
Those who are witnesses, those who testify of Christ, they must be convinced themselves.

128
01:09:08.226 --> 01:09:09.226
You must have seen Him.

129
01:09:18.226 --> 01:09:26.226
And how do we see Him then? We see Him through the Spirit, in how He moves and how He has changed us from the inside and has raised us from the dead.

130
01:09:28.226 --> 01:09:35.226
And in 1 Peter we read, even though you have not seen Him, you love Him.

131
01:09:37.226 --> 01:09:38.226
Peter has seen Him.

132
01:09:39.226 --> 01:09:53.226
Peter has seen Him himself, but he writes to people who have not seen Him and to us, that even though you have not seen Him with your physical eyes, you love Him and you have seen Him and that is why you love Him.

133
01:09:53.226 --> 01:09:56.226
And that is a beautiful reality.

134
01:10:00.226 --> 01:10:02.226
For your reward will be great.

135
01:10:06.226 --> 01:10:10.226
For to believe that you have not seen Him is a greater measure of faith.

136
01:10:11.226 --> 01:10:15.226
So when He sends the Spirit, He does not send the Spirit so that we will just have a nice time.

137
01:10:20.226 --> 01:10:22.226
I love the reception of the Spirit.

138
01:10:27.226 --> 01:10:29.226
I love the reception of the Spirit.

139
01:10:34.226 --> 01:10:36.226
I love the reception of the Spirit.

140
01:10:41.226 --> 01:10:43.226
I love the reception of the Spirit.

141
01:10:48.226 --> 01:10:56.226
I love to worship Him and to exalt Him and that He comes and that His presence rests upon us and we have had that all week and that is wonderful.

142
01:10:57.226 --> 01:11:02.226
But, I know that it is not just about that.

143
01:11:04.226 --> 01:11:06.226
Why does He rest upon us?

144
01:11:07.226 --> 01:11:09.226
Why does He respond?

145
01:11:12.226 --> 01:11:20.226
He wants to give us strength through His Spirit, to be convinced again.

146
01:11:27.226 --> 01:11:31.226
Do you need conviction again, to say, Lord come again?

147
01:11:32.226 --> 01:11:34.226
Still, because we leak.

148
01:11:41.226 --> 01:11:45.226
We are jars that are leaky and we need to be filled.

149
01:11:50.226 --> 01:11:57.226
If 17 years ago was the only moment I would have been filled, then that would have long been gone.

150
01:12:02.226 --> 01:12:10.226
And at our repentance we receive the Spirit, but sometimes that Spirit is still so small in us.

151
01:12:13.226 --> 01:12:16.226
In other words, He has not yet come into us for development.

152
01:12:18.226 --> 01:12:21.226
And that He is still immature in us.

153
01:12:25.226 --> 01:12:30.226
The Spirit is not immature, but I am in my surrender to the Spirit.

154
01:12:32.226 --> 01:12:36.226
He said, it is not so much, Holy Spirit, come more.

155
01:12:38.226 --> 01:12:44.226
But He says, it is more that the Spirit is waiting for us to give ourselves more to Him.

156
01:12:45.226 --> 01:12:47.226
And John Bevere has talked about that.

157
01:12:47.226 --> 01:12:59.226
We do say, Holy Spirit come, and that is okay, but it is much more about the Holy Spirit looking at us and saying, will you surrender more to me so that I can come.

158
01:13:01.226 --> 01:13:03.226
He is without limits, without boundaries.

159
01:13:05.226 --> 01:13:07.226
He is Christ in you.

160
01:13:08.226 --> 01:13:10.226
And He waits to be able to come out.

161
01:13:14.226 --> 01:13:18.226
So this is an encouragement to get moving and to do so through the Holy Spirit.

162
01:13:22.226 --> 01:13:27.226
So this is an encouragement to get moving and to do so through the Holy Spirit.

163
01:13:35.226 --> 01:13:42.226
And I want to mention four things from Acts 2, and it starts with prayer, that prayer attracts the Holy Spirit.

164
01:13:45.226 --> 01:13:47.226
Let's read it, Acts.

165
01:13:48.226 --> 01:13:51.226
Acts 1, verse 4.

166
01:13:55.226 --> 01:13:59.226
And when He was once with them, He commanded them.

167
01:14:04.226 --> 01:14:10.226
And Jesus is speaking to the disciples here and He says, do not leave Jerusalem, but stay there and wait.

168
01:14:11.226 --> 01:14:13.226
Until the promise of the Father.

169
01:14:16.226 --> 01:14:20.226
Until that promise of the Father is fulfilled, which you have heard from me.

170
01:14:25.226 --> 01:14:31.226
And when you read the Gospel of John, you see that Jesus has been preparing them.

171
01:14:32.226 --> 01:14:43.226
And He explains to them, when I go, stay in Jerusalem, do not go out yet.

172
01:14:46.226 --> 01:14:48.226
Without me, you are not that significant.

173
01:14:50.226 --> 01:14:52.226
Without me, you are not that powerful.

174
01:14:52.226 --> 01:15:01.226
You have seen me, you have known me, but you are not that powerful.

175
01:15:02.226 --> 01:15:03.226
Applies to us too, right?

176
01:15:06.226 --> 01:15:09.226
I know Him, but I am really not that powerful.

177
01:15:11.226 --> 01:15:13.226
He says, I want you to wait.

178
01:15:15.226 --> 01:15:17.226
First command, will they do it too?

179
01:15:18.226 --> 01:15:21.226
Can you imagine if they hadn't done that?

180
01:15:23.226 --> 01:15:29.226
And they had to wait, and He doesn't tell them how long they had to wait.

181
01:15:33.226 --> 01:15:38.226
He says, wait and the gift will come in a while.

182
01:15:40.226 --> 01:15:42.226
And that is the first test of faith.

183
01:15:44.226 --> 01:15:45.226
How many have walked away?

184
01:15:48.226 --> 01:15:50.226
In the upper room there were 120 gathered together.

185
01:15:52.226 --> 01:15:54.226
But did it start with 500?

186
01:15:59.226 --> 01:16:04.226
There were 120 left on that day, but how many did they start with? Perhaps many more.

187
01:16:11.226 --> 01:16:14.226
So Jesus ascends and they must wait.

188
01:16:23.226 --> 01:16:24.226
They have no spirit.

189
01:16:25.226 --> 01:16:26.226
How can they speak in tongues?

190
01:16:28.226 --> 01:16:32.226
So Jesus has gone and they go to that upper room and they begin to win.

191
01:16:38.226 --> 01:16:41.226
And they wait and they have no idea how long they must wait.

192
01:16:43.226 --> 01:16:45.226
On day 3 they are still waiting.

193
01:16:47.226 --> 01:16:48.226
Are you still there on day 3?

194
01:16:50.226 --> 01:16:51.226
Are you there on day 4?

195
01:16:53.226 --> 01:16:57.226
Are you there on day 5? You are halfway, but you have no idea of that yet.

196
01:17:00.226 --> 01:17:01.226
Do you still have faith on day 8?

197
01:17:03.226 --> 01:17:04.226
Think about your own life.

198
01:17:09.226 --> 01:17:11.226
What I want to bring us back to is, are we waiting?

199
01:17:13.226 --> 01:17:14.226
Are we waiting for the spirit?

200
01:17:22.226 --> 01:17:34.226
Are you waiting on Monday and on Thursday and taking time each day to wait for the spirit that touches you?

201
01:17:42.226 --> 01:17:50.226
The Bible is never meant to criticize others, but it is meant to reveal our own weakness.

202
01:17:53.226 --> 01:17:56.226
I am weak, in my flesh I am weak, but the Lord says wait.

203
01:18:01.226 --> 01:18:04.226
Wait for the gift that my Father will send.

204
01:18:09.226 --> 01:18:11.226
They were not filled with the power of the Spirit.

205
01:18:16.226 --> 01:18:20.226
And then they come on day 10 and 10 is the number of the test.

206
01:18:23.226 --> 01:18:25.226
And the test was, are they waiting?

207
01:18:28.226 --> 01:18:29.226
Do they have faith?

208
01:18:31.226 --> 01:18:32.226
Will they be obedient?

209
01:18:35.226 --> 01:18:38.226
To receive the Spirit so that they can go out?

210
01:18:42.226 --> 01:18:43.226
And the question is, are we waiting?

211
01:18:46.226 --> 01:18:47.226
Prayer draws the Spirit.

212
01:18:48.226 --> 01:18:50.226
Prayer and waiting are one and the same.

213
01:18:58.226 --> 01:19:01.226
They came to pray and Jesus says wait for me, wait for the Lord.

214
01:19:07.226 --> 01:19:10.226
And one of the meanings of prayer is waiting on the Lord.

215
01:19:18.226 --> 01:19:20.226
And on day 5 it is waiting on the Lord.

216
01:19:24.226 --> 01:19:30.226
And very often on day 5 we walk away, because we say okay Jesus I have waited long enough now, but He says I am almost there, just wait a little longer.

217
01:19:40.226 --> 01:19:46.226
And I want to tell you, it gets easier, because you will recognize His anointing and you will recognize when He comes over you.

218
01:19:48.226 --> 01:19:54.226
In Luke 11 the disciples ask Jesus, teach us to pray.

219
01:20:00.226 --> 01:20:03.226
And then Jesus teaches them the Our Father prayer.

220
01:20:08.226 --> 01:20:11.226
But what He is actually teaching about is perseverance in prayer.

221
01:20:18.226 --> 01:20:19.226
I will not go in.

222
01:20:27.226 --> 01:20:37.226
He then talks about continuing to knock and He gives a whole piece of teaching and He ultimately says keep knocking and the door will be opened, ask and you will receive.

223
01:20:48.226 --> 01:20:57.226
And then He ends by explaining, fathers if your children ask you for something, you know that you want to give it to them, even though you yourselves are evil.

224
01:21:03.226 --> 01:21:09.226
And then He says how much more will the Father give the Spirit to those who ask Him.

225
01:21:09.226 --> 01:21:18.226
So what you will receive the most in your prayer time is more of the Spirit.

226
01:21:25.226 --> 01:21:36.226
And that is what He wants to give us in times of worship, of prayer, of studying the Word. So it’s not that He wants to give us all sorts of things, but He wants to give us more of Himself.

227
01:21:40.226 --> 01:21:42.226
And it starts with prayer.

228
01:21:50.226 --> 01:21:57.226
Coming close to Him in prayer shows that we are building on Him and that we need Him, that we are dependent on Him.

229
01:22:02.226 --> 01:22:06.226
And that is the only place where we will receive more of Him.

230
01:22:10.226 --> 01:22:18.226
And then it continues about the Holy Spirit and the Holy Spirit is the fire of the presence of God.

231
01:22:21.226 --> 01:22:22.226
Acts 1 verse 5

232
01:22:26.226 --> 01:22:28.226
